repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/gnss-log-stats"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  GNSS Log Stats is a small, dependency-free Python command-line tool that
  summarizes an approved GNSS CSV log as JSON: record count, UTC time span,
  latitude/longitude ranges and means, optional altitude, speed, satellite-
  count and HDOP summaries, and counts of recognized fix types. It streams the
  CSV one record at a time, validates explicit-UTC timestamps, coordinate
  ranges and numeric fields, rejects malformed rows, and never echoes
  arbitrary input text or unrecognized fix labels in its output. It runs
  locally and makes no network requests. Scope: descriptive statistics only.
  It does not infer signal conditions, validate a receiver, or establish
  physical evidence. GNSS logs can reveal sensitive location history; no real
  logs are included, and the tests use in-memory sample data.
